    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0980" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg852"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.7512A/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Albania</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hart</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-24T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>10. The Secretary today handed to the Albanian Minister a draft of a proposed
                    treaty of arbitration between the United States and Albania. The provisions of
                    the draft operate to extend the policy of arbitration enunciated in the
                    Arbitration Convention concluded in 1908 between the United States and several
                    other countries. The language of the draft is identical in effect with that of
                    the arbitration treaties recently signed with France and Italy<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d713-f1"/> and with the draft arbitration treaty already submitted
                    to other governments in the general program for the extension of these
                    principles.</p>
                <p>The Secretary also handed to the Minister a proposed draft of a conciliation
                    treaty modeled after so-called Bryan treaties signed by the United States with
                    many countries in 1913 and 1914.</p>
                <p>Full texts are being forwarded in next pouch.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d713-f2"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d713-f1" n="11" xml:id="d713-f1-content">
                <p>See <ref target="frus1928v02#pg_816">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>,
                        pp. 816</ref> ff and <ref target="frus1928v03#pg_102">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 102</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d713-f2" n="12" xml:id="d713-f2-content">
                <p>Drafts not printed; both treaties were signed without change.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
